4. Methodology

1. Safe sample selection — a synthetic phishing email was created using only .test domains and documentation IP ranges (185.220.101.45, 192.168.1.100). No real victim emails were used.
2. Static parsing — the .eml is read as raw bytes and decoded. Headers and body are separated on the first blank line.
3. Regex extraction — each IOC type has a dedicated compiled regex.
4. Risk analysis — sender vs Reply-To comparison, SPF/DKIM/DMARC header scanning, TLD reputation checks.
5. Reporting — results printed to terminal in a structured format.

