9. Remediation

· Block paypal-alerts.test and other-domain.test at DNS/proxy
· Add 185.220.101.45 to block lists after reputation check
· Enforce DMARC p=reject, SPF and DKIM on company domains
· Enable advanced phishing protection on the mail gateway
· Train users to check Reply-To and hover over links
· Alert on Reply-To ≠ From mismatches and suspicious TLDs

---

10. Lessons Learned

· Regex is powerful but limited — matches are evidence, not proof of malice
· Static analysis is safer than dynamic — never open links or attachments
· Header anomalies (Reply-To mismatch + SPF fail) are strong phishing signals
· Python's standard library covers a complete analyzer without dependencies
· Documentation matters — findings, evidence and remediation are part of the deliverable

